# deliberate-reasoning-layer slice 1 — metacognitive gate +
evidence-bound re-entrant loop + pre-registered experiment — apply ladder

Per `docs/plans/metacognitive-gate-reentrant-loop-slice1.md` (RATIFIED
@ c0c584f4) — implements §4 of the source proposal
`workspace/.scratch/claude-output/consciousness-emulation-harness-design.md`
(the smallest viable first experiment: the gate + the evidence-bound
re-entrant loop), with the §0 honest-boundary carried as a HARD
pre-registration requirement.

Scope (plan §2 + §5 + §7): NEW component
`framework/deliberate-reasoning/`. A turn-level GATE decides per-turn
whether the fast inference path answers (don't-escalate) or a
DELIBERATE, evidence-bound, re-entrant LOOP engages — default OFF,
escalating only on a defined observable trigger set (low_confidence,
novelty, stakes — all three per the dispatcher's D-MGRL.4 ruling). A
PRE-REGISTERED experiment fixes the metric, task set, blind-judge
protocol, and the theory-prediction-vs-generic-lift discriminator
BEFORE any scored run.

AC families (plan §5):

  - AC.MGRL.1 — deterministic, LLM-free gate (D-MGRL.1): escalate /
    don't-escalate + the firing trigger, from observable signals, no
    LLM call on the don't-escalate path. Sibling in shape to
    intent_classifier.py.
  - AC.MGRL.2 — default-OFF no-op (D-MGRL.5): a non-escalated turn
    returns the draft byte-identical; the critic is never called (no
    deliberate-loop tokens spent).
  - AC.MGRL.3 — the deliberate loop (D-MGRL.2): draft → adversarial
    evidence-bound critique → revise → re-check, with a NO-DEGRADATION
    guard that returns the original draft when critique finds no
    evidence-backed improvement. The structural answer to the proposal
    §3 always-on-self-critique-degrades trap.
  - AC.MGRL.4 — pre-registration (D-MGRL.3): the artefact fixes the
    task set, metric definitions, "better", and the theory-vs-generic
    discriminator; the pre-reg commit is an ancestor of the first
    scored-run commit (git-ancestry tamper-evidence,
    feedback_published_state_only_from_git_refs).
  - AC.MGRL.5 — blind judge: the scorer's signature
    (prompt, answer, canonical_answer) structurally excludes any
    arm/hypothesis label; baseline-vs-escalated scored blind.
  - AC.MGRL.6 — the result reports the aggregate generic-lift delta AND
    the flagged-vs-unflagged theory discriminator SEPARATELY; "the
    theory's prediction held" is a distinct verdict from "escalation
    helped on average".
  - AC.MGRL.7 — ships default-OFF: a single explicit reversible opt-in
    (LOAM_DELIBERATE_REASONING env var / TurnConfig flag); off =>
    harness unchanged.
  - AC.MGRL.OA ★ (outcome-altitude) — escalation fires through the
    production entry-point (process_turn) with NO pre-arranged state:
    a real turn carrying a genuine trigger signal yields an escalation
    decision + a deliberate-loop invocation + a recorded firing trigger
    (feedback_test_outcome_altitude_required).

Method-level choices are the builder's call per ODD §1.1; the plan
fixed the ACs (§5), the named decisions (D-MGRL.1..5), the fence (§7),
and the halt triggers (§8), not the implementation.

HONEST-BOUNDARY note (plan §0 / §8 trigger 2, NON-NEGOTIABLE): the
pre-registered metric is exact-match correctness against a
machine-checkable canonical answer over a FROZEN task set — objective
and non-gameable (subjective-quality tasks were deliberately excluded).
The bundled reference experiment run uses a deterministic, evidence-
bound reference critic with access to the answer key; it demonstrates
the harness + discriminator MECHANICS end-to-end (verdict
THEORY-PREDICTION-CONFIRMED on the reference run), NOT a theory
confirmation on a real model. A real confirmation requires the
LLM-critic run (claude -p, the slice's optional follow-on per
PRE_REGISTRATION §6) over the identical task set + judge + verdict rule.
A null or generic-lift-only result remains a VALID outcome (RF-3).

